  "body": {
    "id": "lem:gap-variance-inheritance",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For every \\(s\\in\\mathcal S\\), \\(V_s^{\\mathrm{gap}}=(1-\\varrho)^{-1}\\operatorname{Var}(A_s)+r\\operatorname{Var}(R_s)=V_s+\\{\\varrho/(1-\\varrho)\\}\\operatorname{Var}(A_s)\\geq V_s\\geq\\nu\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "s",
      "S",
      "Vgaps",
      "varrho",
      "As",
      "r",
      "Rs",
      "Vs",
      "nu"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:att-variance-margin"
    ],
    "justification": "The corrected estimator needs no additional primitive variance assumption beyond the conventional fixed-role marginal margin.",
    "gap": "Scalar HAC positivity for the retained blocks is inherited algebraically here rather than imposed as a separate condition.",
    "consumer": "It licenses coordinate-wise studentization of either early-selected role in the uniform split-sample question.",
    "proof_tex": "By the definition of \\(V_s^{\\mathrm{gap}}\\) and the definition of \\(V_s\\),\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nV_s^{\\mathrm{gap}}-V_s\n&=\\left\\{(1-\\varrho)^{-1}-1\\right\\}\\operatorname{Var}(A_s)\n  +r\\operatorname{Var}(R_s)-r\\operatorname{Var}(R_s)\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\varrho}{1-\\varrho}\\operatorname{Var}(A_s).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe declared restriction \\(0<\\varrho<1\\) makes \\(\\varrho/(1-\\varrho)>0\\), and every variance is nonnegative.  Consequently\n\\[\nV_s^{\\mathrm{gap}}=V_s+\\frac{\\varrho}{1-\\varrho}\\operatorname{Var}(A_s)\\geq V_s.\n\\]\nAssumption \\(\\mathrm{ass{:}att\\mbox{-}variance\\mbox{-}margin}\\) states, separately for each \\(s\\in\\mathcal S\\), that \\(V_s\\geq\\nu\\).  Combining the last two displays proves the claim for both roles.  No rank or joint-covariance inversion is used.",
